1
00:00:37,162 --> 00:00:38,913
<i>NARRATOR: 
Five thousand years ago,</i>

2
00:00:38,955 --> 00:00:42,167
<i>a fierce warrior 
known as the Scorpion King</i>

3
00:00:42,250 --> 00:00:44,294
<i>led a great army on a campaign</i>

4
00:00:44,377 --> 00:00:46,504
<i>to conquer the known world.</i>

5
00:00:54,971 --> 00:00:56,639
(ALL SHOUTING)

6
00:01:05,482 --> 00:01:08,068
(SPEAKING IN 
ANCIENT EGYPTIAN LANGUAGE)

7
00:01:18,703 --> 00:01:20,038
(SHOUTING)

8
00:02:07,710 --> 00:02:12,423
<i>NARRATOR: 
After a vicious campaign 
which lasted seven long years,</i>

9
00:02:12,507 --> 00:02:15,552
<i>the Scorpion King and his army 
were defeated</i>

10
00:02:15,635 --> 00:02:19,305
<i>and driven deep 
into the sacred desert 
of Ahm Shere.</i>

11
00:02:32,485 --> 00:02:34,320
(BIRD SCREECHING)

12
00:02:41,786 --> 00:02:46,040
<i>One by one, 
they slowly perished 
under the scorching sun</i>

13
00:02:48,459 --> 00:02:52,130
<i>until only 
the great warrior himself 
was left alive.</i>

14
00:02:59,262 --> 00:03:01,014
<i>Near death,</i>

15
00:03:01,097 --> 00:03:05,059
<i>the Scorpion King made a pact 
with the dark god Anubis</i>

16
00:03:05,810 --> 00:03:07,937
<i>that if Anubis 
would spare his life</i>

17
00:03:08,021 --> 00:03:10,398
<i>and let him conquer 
his enemies,</i>

18
00:03:10,773 --> 00:03:12,942
<i>he would give him his soul.</i>

19
00:03:20,825 --> 00:03:24,787
<i>Anubis accepted his offer 
and spared his life.</i>

20
00:03:44,766 --> 00:03:47,018
(YELLING)

21
00:03:52,273 --> 00:03:55,151
<i>Anubis gave the Scorpion King 
command of his army,</i>

22
00:03:55,276 --> 00:03:56,611
(GROWLING)

23
00:03:57,528 --> 00:04:02,242
<i>And like an evil flood, 
they washed away 
all that lay before them.</i>

24
00:04:03,868 --> 00:04:05,536
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

25
00:04:13,294 --> 00:04:17,048
<i>When his task was done, 
Anubis forced 
the Scorpion King</i>

26
00:04:17,131 --> 00:04:19,342
<i>to serve him for all time.</i>

27
00:04:19,676 --> 00:04:21,052
(GRUNTS)

28
00:04:26,349 --> 00:04:30,270
<i>His army was returned 
to the sands 
from whence they came,</i>

29
00:04:30,436 --> 00:04:31,896
(GROWLING)

30
00:04:35,024 --> 00:04:38,194
<i>Where they wait, silently,</i>

31
00:04:38,236 --> 00:04:40,446
<i>to be awakened once again.</i>

32
00:05:02,719 --> 00:05:04,387
(MICE SQUEAKING)

33
00:05:09,851 --> 00:05:11,602
(GUN COCKING)

34
00:06:04,781 --> 00:06:06,115
(SNARLING)

35
00:06:12,622 --> 00:06:14,582
(BOTH SCREAM)

36
00:06:17,168 --> 00:06:18,336
Alex?

37
00:06:19,796 --> 00:06:22,465
What were you thinking, 
a mummy had come back 
to life?

38
00:06:22,507 --> 00:06:24,300
I'll tell you 
a story sometime.

39
00:06:24,383 --> 00:06:26,886
What are you doing down here? 
I told you to wait for us 
up in the temple.

40
00:06:26,969 --> 00:06:27,970
But, Dad, I saw... 
No "buts."

41
00:06:28,012 --> 00:06:29,097
It's dangerous down here, 
Alex.

42
00:06:29,138 --> 00:06:31,808
But I saw your tattoo. 
You saw what?

43
00:06:31,891 --> 00:06:34,977
On a wall by the entrance. 
There's a cartouche 
just like it.

44
00:06:35,019 --> 00:06:39,315
With the pyramid and the eye 
and the two kings 
and everything.

45
00:06:39,732 --> 00:06:41,734
Really? 
Yeah.

46
00:06:41,818 --> 00:06:44,737
Okay, well, 
I'll be up to take a look 
at that in a minute.

47
00:06:44,821 --> 00:06:46,614
In the meantime, 
I want you to wait for us 
up there.

48
00:06:46,656 --> 00:06:47,740
But... But...

49
00:06:47,824 --> 00:06:51,244
No, pick up your stuff, 
and I'll see you up 
in the temple. Go.

50
00:06:52,787 --> 00:06:56,082
Go on. 
And... 
And what shall I do?

51
00:06:56,165 --> 00:06:58,626
I don't know. Surprise me.

52
00:06:59,085 --> 00:07:01,421
Build a better mousetrap. 
Okay.

53
00:07:01,504 --> 00:07:04,340
While your mother 
goes and desecrates 
another tomb.

54
00:07:11,681 --> 00:07:13,808
(HISSING)

55
00:07:18,312 --> 00:07:19,689
Go away.

56
00:07:20,648 --> 00:07:21,774
(GASPS)

57
00:07:22,650 --> 00:07:25,570
Those are poisonous, 
you know. 
Only if they bite you.

58
00:07:25,653 --> 00:07:28,239
What was all that about? 
Oh, nothing.

59
00:07:28,322 --> 00:07:30,950
Alex wanted 
to show me something.

60
00:07:31,033 --> 00:07:33,035
I swear,

61
00:07:33,077 --> 00:07:35,580
the kid gets more and more 
like you every day.

62
00:07:35,663 --> 00:07:40,042
What, 
you mean more attractive, 
sweet and devilishly charming?

63
00:07:40,126 --> 00:07:42,378
No, he's driving me crazy.

64
00:07:42,837 --> 00:07:44,589
Now, where were we?

65
00:07:45,631 --> 00:07:47,341
Hammer and chisel.

66
00:07:52,305 --> 00:07:55,766
All right, all right! 
Let's do it your way. 
Thank you.

67
00:07:59,020 --> 00:08:00,771
(THUDDING)

68
00:08:14,660 --> 00:08:20,082
Ever since I had that dream, 
this place is 
all I can think about.

69
00:08:20,124 --> 00:08:24,420
Ever since you had that dream, 
I haven't had a decent night 
of sleep.

70
00:08:24,921 --> 00:08:27,381
EVELYN: I feel like 
I've been here before.

71
00:08:27,757 --> 00:08:31,469
I know I've been here before. 
Evy, 
nobody's been here before.

72
00:08:31,552 --> 00:08:34,805
Not in at least 3,000 years. 
Except for these guys.

73
00:08:40,102 --> 00:08:42,605
Then how do I seem to know 
exactly where I'm going?

74
00:08:57,370 --> 00:08:58,621
MAN: Let's go.

75
00:09:01,832 --> 00:09:03,626
(MICE SQUEAKING)

76
00:09:15,304 --> 00:09:17,098
(VOICES ECHOING)

77
00:09:32,780 --> 00:09:36,200
Knock, knock. Anybody home?

78
00:09:39,287 --> 00:09:42,456
You two check out that stuff, 
see if it's there.

79
00:09:42,707 --> 00:09:44,959
I'll sort out the O'Connells.

80
00:11:18,135 --> 00:11:21,222
You know, if you move that 
fast enough, you can almost 
write your name.

81
00:11:21,263 --> 00:11:23,099
I just had a vision.

82
00:11:23,557 --> 00:11:27,686
It was... 
It was like my dream, 
but it was real.

83
00:11:27,770 --> 00:11:30,147
It was like 
I was actually here 
in ancient times.

84
00:11:30,231 --> 00:11:34,777
Well, if you actually 
were here, could you show me 
how to open this thing?

85
00:11:35,403 --> 00:11:36,779
Hold this.

86
00:11:52,002 --> 00:11:55,881
All right, now you're 
starting to scare me. 
Now I'm starting 
to scare myself.

87
00:11:56,757 --> 00:11:59,718
What is this? 
Look at the state 
of this rubbish.

88
00:11:59,802 --> 00:12:03,556
Those Egyptians 
never had a clue. 
It's all chintz and stuff.

89
00:12:04,098 --> 00:12:05,474
Look at that.

90
00:12:05,558 --> 00:12:09,687
Cheap pottery, this. 
Ancient rubbish.

91
00:12:09,937 --> 00:12:11,105
(SCREAMING)

92
00:12:11,147 --> 00:12:12,356
(GUN COCKING)

93
00:12:12,440 --> 00:12:18,154
Jacques, 
something's hit me head! 
Shut up, Spivey. 
This place is cursed.

94
00:12:21,157 --> 00:12:23,367
We do not want 
to wake the gods.

95
00:12:37,715 --> 00:12:39,300
(GROANING)

96
00:12:45,473 --> 00:12:48,142
EVELYN: That's the emblem 
of the Scorpion King.

97
00:12:48,184 --> 00:12:50,352
He's supposed to be pure myth.

98
00:12:50,436 --> 00:12:53,147
No... No trace of him 
has ever been found before.

99
00:12:53,189 --> 00:12:56,192
No artifacts, 
no archival evidence.

100
00:12:56,442 --> 00:12:58,194
Maybe they didn't want 
anybody to find him.

101
00:12:58,235 --> 00:12:59,278
Let's open this.

102
00:12:59,361 --> 00:13:02,072
Evy, I don't have 
a real good feeling 
about this.

103
00:13:02,156 --> 00:13:05,534
It's only a chest. 
No harm ever came 
from opening a chest.

104
00:13:05,576 --> 00:13:08,037
Right, 
and no harm ever came 
from reading a book.

105
00:13:08,078 --> 00:13:10,706
Remember how that went? 
We can't stop now.

106
00:13:10,748 --> 00:13:13,375
Just remember, 
I was the voice 
of reason here.

107
00:13:13,459 --> 00:13:14,543
For once.

108
00:13:14,627 --> 00:13:18,923
Rubbish. Rubbish. 
Dreck. Chintz.

109
00:13:19,381 --> 00:13:20,883
Only half of this...

110
00:13:20,966 --> 00:13:22,426
(GROANING)

111
00:13:24,303 --> 00:13:25,888
(LAUGHING) 
God, that hurt!

112
00:13:45,366 --> 00:13:48,786
Hon? Let's do it your way.

113
00:14:06,845 --> 00:14:09,014
The bracelet of Anubis.

114
00:14:17,273 --> 00:14:19,233
I'll take care of this.

115
00:14:20,901 --> 00:14:22,194
(GUN COCKING)

116
00:14:22,444 --> 00:14:23,988
(RUMBLING)

117
00:14:25,698 --> 00:14:27,283
Oh, my God.

118
00:14:28,409 --> 00:14:30,452
It's a bit late for that!

119
00:14:30,661 --> 00:14:33,622
Put it in your rucksack. 
I got a better idea. 
Let's leave it here.

120
00:14:33,706 --> 00:14:36,208
I think 
it's a bit late for that! 
What's it say?

121
00:14:36,292 --> 00:14:41,630
"He who disturbs this bracelet 
shall drink from the Nile."

122
00:14:41,672 --> 00:14:43,257
That doesn't sound too bad.

123
00:14:44,800 --> 00:14:46,302
(SCREAMING)

124
00:15:01,650 --> 00:15:05,905
Jacques's gonna make 
a nice fillet out of you, 
my son.

125
00:15:07,364 --> 00:15:10,326
Oh, please. Please. 
Spivey! Jacques!

126
00:15:10,659 --> 00:15:13,829
Let's get the hell 
out of here! 
Come on!

127
00:15:19,877 --> 00:15:21,629
Come on!

128
00:15:31,513 --> 00:15:33,015
(GRUNTS)

129
00:15:37,895 --> 00:15:39,188
(SCREAMS)

130
00:15:40,731 --> 00:15:42,399
(BOTH SCREAMING)

131
00:15:43,984 --> 00:15:45,486
(GRUNTING)

132
00:16:06,215 --> 00:16:07,383
Whoa.

133
00:16:33,283 --> 00:16:35,077
(BOTH SCREAMING)

134
00:16:45,504 --> 00:16:47,172
(BOTH COUGHING)

135
00:16:47,506 --> 00:16:51,552
Mom, Dad, 
I can explain everything.

136
00:17:19,246 --> 00:17:22,207
<i>The Book of the Dead</i> 
gives life.

137
00:17:22,750 --> 00:17:25,127
And <i>The Book of the Living</i>

138
00:17:27,296 --> 00:17:29,423
takes life away.

139
00:17:29,798 --> 00:17:32,092
I thought that was my job.

140
00:17:34,720 --> 00:17:36,430
We're getting close.

141
00:17:37,848 --> 00:17:39,433
(MEN CHATTERING)

142
00:18:06,251 --> 00:18:07,961
Did you acquire it?

143
00:18:08,045 --> 00:18:10,380
(RUMBLING)

144
00:18:27,189 --> 00:18:28,857
(HORSE WHINNYING)

145
00:18:48,293 --> 00:18:50,379
(SKITTERING)

146
00:18:50,462 --> 00:18:52,840
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

147
00:19:01,306 --> 00:19:03,559
We're getting very close.

148
00:19:08,856 --> 00:19:10,274
(SKITTERING)

149
00:19:18,323 --> 00:19:19,950
We've found him.

150
00:19:22,244 --> 00:19:24,746
We've found him! 
We've found him!

151
00:19:41,930 --> 00:19:44,308
Step aside here. 
Out of the way!

152
00:19:49,563 --> 00:19:53,442
Imhotep. It's him. 
It's Imhotep.

153
00:19:58,530 --> 00:20:00,324
Now we must raise 
those that serve him.

154
00:20:00,407 --> 00:20:01,575
(MAN 1 SPEAKING ARABIC) 
MAN 2: Get out of my way.

155
00:20:01,617 --> 00:20:05,370
Get out of my way, 
or I'm gonna shoot you 
in the face.

156
00:20:05,454 --> 00:20:07,956
He means it. 
He shot someone before.

157
00:20:08,040 --> 00:20:12,711
Give it to me. 
The opportunity passed us by.

158
00:20:13,629 --> 00:20:15,464
We need that bracelet.

159
00:20:15,505 --> 00:20:18,091
And we need it 
before it opens.

160
00:20:22,137 --> 00:20:23,597
Enough.

161
00:20:25,849 --> 00:20:30,896
My dear Hafez, 
I told you I should have 
handled it.

162
00:20:30,979 --> 00:20:35,275
I did not want 
your past history 
to cloud the issue.

163
00:20:35,317 --> 00:20:37,986
We know where it is. 
We'll take care of it.

164
00:20:38,028 --> 00:20:40,197
No, we'll take care of it.

165
00:20:40,739 --> 00:20:43,575
I have a different chore 
for you now.

166
00:20:43,659 --> 00:20:47,537
Where is the bracelet? 
It's on its way 
to merry old London.

167
00:20:49,081 --> 00:20:51,500
Then London 
is where we must go.

168
00:21:09,351 --> 00:21:11,228
The last known expedition 
to actually

169
00:21:11,270 --> 00:21:14,398
reach Ahm Shere 
was sent by Ramses IV

170
00:21:14,481 --> 00:21:16,274
over 3,000 years ago.

171
00:21:16,358 --> 00:21:19,069
He sent over a thousand men. 
And none of them 
was ever seen again.

172
00:21:19,152 --> 00:21:21,196
How did you know? 
I didn't. 
But that's always the story.

173
00:21:21,238 --> 00:21:23,699
Did I mention 
there was a pyramid of gold? 
Twice.

174
00:21:23,740 --> 00:21:26,118
Alexander the Great 
sent troops in search of it.

175
00:21:26,201 --> 00:21:27,911
Hooray for him. 
So did Caesar.

176
00:21:27,953 --> 00:21:30,080
Yeah, look what happened 
to his career. 
And Napoleon.

177
00:21:30,122 --> 00:21:33,417
But we're smarter than him. 
And taller, too.

178
00:21:33,500 --> 00:21:37,254
Exactly. That's why 
we're gonna find it. 
Because we're taller?

179
00:21:38,422 --> 00:21:41,383
That's why I love you. 
Nice try.

180
00:21:42,718 --> 00:21:44,428
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

181
00:22:02,362 --> 00:22:03,655
ALEX: Mom!

182
00:22:04,156 --> 00:22:05,907
What do I do with this chest?

183
00:22:05,949 --> 00:22:08,160
This sucker weighs 
a goddang ton.

184
00:22:08,243 --> 00:22:10,329
Alex, watch your language!

185
00:22:10,412 --> 00:22:12,247
Rather weighty, this.

186
00:22:16,334 --> 00:22:17,544
(CLICKING)

187
00:22:17,627 --> 00:22:18,962
Huh?

188
00:22:21,882 --> 00:22:25,802
Evy, that first weird dream 
of yours was exactly 
six weeks ago, right?

189
00:22:25,844 --> 00:22:29,014
I think so, yes. 
But what's that got to do 
with anything?

190
00:22:29,556 --> 00:22:33,060
It just happens to coincide 
with Egyptian New Year.

191
00:22:33,727 --> 00:22:36,855
Oh. That's right. 
What a coincidence.

192
00:22:38,357 --> 00:22:42,778
Maybe. All I'm saying is, 
let's be cautious.

193
00:22:47,574 --> 00:22:49,034
Oh!

194
00:22:51,578 --> 00:22:55,248
If anything happened to you, 
I would never forgive myself.

195
00:22:59,669 --> 00:23:01,213
(GASPS)

196
00:23:01,505 --> 00:23:02,923
(SNARLING)

197
00:23:15,352 --> 00:23:18,105
You and Alex 
are the only thing 
that matter to me.

198
00:23:18,188 --> 00:23:19,606
Well,

199
00:23:20,816 --> 00:23:24,361
the Bembridge scholars 
have been begging me

200
00:23:24,402 --> 00:23:26,446
to run the British Museum.

201
00:23:35,122 --> 00:23:37,124
Wh... Whoa.

202
00:23:44,631 --> 00:23:47,217
Hey, Alex, 
behave yourself 
for five minutes.

203
00:23:47,801 --> 00:23:49,219
You betcha.

204
00:23:58,270 --> 00:24:00,981
Happy to be home? 
Couldn't be happier.

205
00:24:01,815 --> 00:24:04,192
It's the year of the scorpion.

206
00:24:04,276 --> 00:24:06,445
Neat! 
Thought you might like that.

207
00:24:06,987 --> 00:24:10,615
So then I killed the mummy 
and all his minions 
and stole his scepter.

208
00:24:10,657 --> 00:24:14,578
Oh, you're so brave. 
And rich. 
Did I mention rich?

209
00:24:14,619 --> 00:24:16,746
What do you think 
I'm doing here?

210
00:24:19,291 --> 00:24:21,126
Sorry. We must be 
in the wrong house.

211
00:24:21,168 --> 00:24:23,879
You said 
this was your house. 
No, I didn't.

212
00:24:23,962 --> 00:24:25,630
Call me!

213
00:24:26,590 --> 00:24:29,092
You're not Sheila's husband, 
are you? 
No.

214
00:24:29,718 --> 00:24:32,888
Mr. O'Connell, 
you try my patience.

215
00:24:32,971 --> 00:24:36,183
Mr. O'Connell? 
No, hold on a minute. 
You've got the wrong...

216
00:24:36,266 --> 00:24:38,476
That bracelet. 
Now I remember.

217
00:24:38,518 --> 00:24:42,189
I lost it in a card game. 
For your sake, I hope not.

218
00:24:46,151 --> 00:24:47,652
It can't be.

219
00:24:48,695 --> 00:24:50,363
ANCK-SU-NAMUN: Hello.

220
00:24:53,533 --> 00:24:54,910
Hello.

221
00:24:55,660 --> 00:24:59,372
Where's your wife? 
My wife? Oh, you mean Evy.

222
00:24:59,456 --> 00:25:03,001
I think she went off 
to Baden-Baden 
or Tibet or something.

223
00:25:03,043 --> 00:25:04,544
The girl's a free spirit.

224
00:25:04,586 --> 00:25:06,922
Did I mention 
I was single now?

225
00:25:11,593 --> 00:25:12,636
(HISSING)

226
00:25:12,719 --> 00:25:15,597
Egyptian asps 
are quite poisonous.

227
00:25:16,598 --> 00:25:18,099
It's downstairs. 
There's a safe.

228
00:25:18,183 --> 00:25:22,729
The combination is 320-58...

229
00:25:22,812 --> 00:25:24,940
393-something.

230
00:25:25,023 --> 00:25:28,235
It's in a safe downstairs. 
I told you. I told you!

231
00:25:28,318 --> 00:25:29,528
And your point is?

232
00:25:29,569 --> 00:25:31,863
My point is, 
I told you so you 
wouldn't kill me.

233
00:25:31,905 --> 00:25:34,407
When did we make 
that arrangement?

234
00:25:38,578 --> 00:25:39,829
Hello.

235
00:25:41,373 --> 00:25:44,793
Alex, I'm serious. 
If you've lost that key, 
you're grounded.

236
00:25:44,834 --> 00:25:47,837
I haven't lost it. 
I just can't find it. 
There's a difference.

237
00:25:47,879 --> 00:25:50,674
Well, you'd better start 
finding it then.

238
00:25:50,757 --> 00:25:53,134
I will, Mom. 
There's nothing 
to worry about.

239
00:25:53,176 --> 00:25:54,678
Good evening.

240
00:25:57,639 --> 00:26:01,184
Who are you? 
What are you doing here?

241
00:26:01,268 --> 00:26:03,937
I'm looking for the chest, 
of course.

242
00:26:05,897 --> 00:26:07,607
Give it to me now.

243
00:26:10,443 --> 00:26:13,363
Get out of my house.

244
00:26:13,446 --> 00:26:15,699
Whoa, Mom. 
Maybe not the best idea.

245
00:26:15,740 --> 00:26:17,534
Alex, get back there.

246
00:26:20,787 --> 00:26:23,331
Definitely not 
the best idea.

247
00:26:23,373 --> 00:26:25,166
I think it's time to yell 
for Dad now.

248
00:26:25,208 --> 00:26:28,837
Now I will kill you 
and take it anyway. 
ARDETH: I think not.

249
00:26:31,047 --> 00:26:34,009
Ardeth, 
what are you doing here?

250
00:26:34,050 --> 00:26:36,094
Perhaps explanations 
are best kept for later.

251
00:26:36,177 --> 00:26:37,762
Ardeth Bay.

252
00:26:38,263 --> 00:26:39,556
Lock-Nah.

253
00:26:40,765 --> 00:26:41,891
Knowing my brother-in-law,

254
00:26:41,975 --> 00:26:44,019
he probably deserves 
whatever you're about 
to do to him,

255
00:26:44,060 --> 00:26:48,148
but this is my house, 
I have certain rules about 
snakes and dismemberment.

256
00:26:51,901 --> 00:26:53,153
Shoot him!

257
00:26:54,738 --> 00:26:56,948
(SPEAKING ARABIC)

258
00:27:16,760 --> 00:27:20,096
Whoa, Mom! 
When did you learn to do that?

259
00:27:20,180 --> 00:27:21,765
I have no idea.

260
00:27:27,103 --> 00:27:28,480
That I learned 
from your father.

261
00:27:30,857 --> 00:27:33,276
I'll take that. 
Whoa!

262
00:27:42,285 --> 00:27:45,205
Not bad for a Medjai.

263
00:27:52,087 --> 00:27:53,296
Let go!

264
00:28:02,764 --> 00:28:05,809
What's in the chest? 
The bracelet of Anubis!

265
00:28:20,198 --> 00:28:23,993
They must not 
get the bracelet! 
Get it and get out of here!

266
00:28:30,500 --> 00:28:32,043
Mom, look out!

267
00:28:32,836 --> 00:28:34,212
Evelyn!

268
00:28:38,758 --> 00:28:39,843
Mom!

269
00:29:06,119 --> 00:29:07,245
Rick!

270
00:29:08,288 --> 00:29:10,248
Evelyn! 
Look out, Rick!

271
00:29:20,633 --> 00:29:22,552
Dad! Dad!

272
00:29:23,470 --> 00:29:25,054
Are you all right? 
Yeah.

273
00:29:25,138 --> 00:29:26,598
Yeah? Okay.

274
00:29:28,308 --> 00:29:29,684
O'Connell.

275
00:29:31,060 --> 00:29:34,189
What are you doing here? 
No, scratch that. 
I don't care.

276
00:29:34,230 --> 00:29:36,149
Who are those guys? 
Where are they taking my wife?

277
00:29:36,232 --> 00:29:38,902
My friend, I'm not sure,

278
00:29:38,985 --> 00:29:42,906
but wherever this man is, 
your wife will surely be.

279
00:29:44,699 --> 00:29:46,451
Hey, I know him.

280
00:29:46,534 --> 00:29:49,412
He's the curator. 
He works at 
the British Museum.

281
00:29:49,496 --> 00:29:51,289
Are you sure? 
Believe him.

282
00:29:51,372 --> 00:29:54,083
He spends more time there 
than at home.

283
00:29:56,336 --> 00:29:58,922
You're here, 
the bad guys are here, 
Evy's been kidnapped.

284
00:29:58,963 --> 00:30:00,924
Let me guess. 
Yes, they once again removed

285
00:30:01,007 --> 00:30:02,133
the creature from his grave.

286
00:30:02,217 --> 00:30:03,259
I don't mean 
to point fingers,

287
00:30:03,343 --> 00:30:05,595
but isn't it your job 
to make sure 
that doesn't happen?

288
00:30:05,678 --> 00:30:07,347
That woman who was with him, 
she knows things

289
00:30:07,430 --> 00:30:09,265
that no living person 
could possibly know.

290
00:30:09,349 --> 00:30:11,559
She knew exactly 
where the creature 
was buried.

291
00:30:11,601 --> 00:30:14,771
We were hoping she would 
lead us to the bracelet. 
She obviously did.

292
00:30:14,854 --> 00:30:16,356
And now they have it.

293
00:30:16,439 --> 00:30:18,858
I wouldn't get 
too nervous just yet.

294
00:30:21,069 --> 00:30:22,195
Is that gold?

295
00:30:22,278 --> 00:30:24,364
When I stuck it on, 
I saw the pyramids at Giza.

296
00:30:24,447 --> 00:30:27,283
Then, whoosh! 
Straight across 
the desert to Karnak.

297
00:30:27,325 --> 00:30:29,202
By putting this on, 
you have started 
a chain reaction

298
00:30:29,285 --> 00:30:31,538
that could bring 
the next apocalypse.

299
00:30:31,913 --> 00:30:36,000
You, lighten up. 
You, big trouble. 
You, get in the car.

300
00:30:42,090 --> 00:30:43,842
I am sorry 
if I alarmed your son,

301
00:30:43,925 --> 00:30:46,970
but you must understand, 
now that the bracelet 
is on his wrist,

302
00:30:47,011 --> 00:30:49,222
we have only seven days before 
the Scorpion King awakens.

303
00:30:53,476 --> 00:30:55,603
Whomever can kill 
the Scorpion King

304
00:30:55,645 --> 00:30:57,564
can send his army back 
to the Underworld

305
00:30:57,605 --> 00:31:00,358
or use it to destroy mankind 
and rule the Earth.

306
00:31:00,441 --> 00:31:01,943
That's why 
they dug up Imhotep.

307
00:31:01,985 --> 00:31:04,362
He's the only guy tough enough 
to take out the Scorpion King.

308
00:31:04,445 --> 00:31:05,613
That is their plan.

309
00:31:18,251 --> 00:31:21,796
Alex, 
I've got a big job for you. 
Stay here and protect the car.

310
00:31:21,879 --> 00:31:24,465
I can do that. 
Protect the car?

311
00:31:24,549 --> 00:31:27,343
Just because I'm a kid 
doesn't mean I'm stupid.

312
00:31:27,427 --> 00:31:29,888
I know. 
Dad!

313
00:31:30,680 --> 00:31:34,058
If you see anyone 
come out screaming, 
it's just me.

314
00:31:34,142 --> 00:31:37,812
Maybe you should stay here 
and watch him. 
Yes, now you're talking.

315
00:31:42,025 --> 00:31:45,320
You want the shotgun? 
No, I prefer the Thompson.

316
00:31:51,951 --> 00:31:53,620
If I were to say to you,

317
00:31:53,661 --> 00:31:57,832
I'm a stranger 
traveling from the east, 
seeking that which is lost...

318
00:31:57,874 --> 00:32:00,668
Then I would reply 
that I am a stranger 
traveling from the west.

319
00:32:00,710 --> 00:32:04,172
It is I whom you seek. How... 
Then it is true.

320
00:32:04,213 --> 00:32:06,674
You have the sacred mark. 
What, that?

321
00:32:06,716 --> 00:32:09,177
No, that got slapped on me 
in an orphanage in Cairo.

322
00:32:09,260 --> 00:32:14,682
That mark means 
you're a protector of man, 
a warrior for God, a Medjai.

323
00:32:14,724 --> 00:32:16,809
(GUN COCKING) 
Sorry. 
You've got the wrong guy.

324
00:32:20,063 --> 00:32:22,982
(PEOPLE CHANTING)

325
00:32:52,011 --> 00:32:55,056
(HAFEZ CHANTING 
IN ANCIENT EGYPTIAN LANGUAGE)

326
00:33:01,896 --> 00:33:03,272
Mr. Hafez.

327
00:33:08,403 --> 00:33:09,987
They found him.

328
00:33:31,426 --> 00:33:33,928
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

329
00:33:52,905 --> 00:33:55,324
(ROARING)

330
00:34:10,173 --> 00:34:13,593
(HAFEZ CHANTING 
IN ANCIENT EGYPTIAN LANGUAGE)

331
00:34:33,821 --> 00:34:35,114
(GROWLING)

332
00:34:45,666 --> 00:34:46,959
Imhotep.

333
00:34:47,835 --> 00:34:50,421
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

334
00:34:57,512 --> 00:34:59,180
(LAUGHING)

335
00:34:59,263 --> 00:35:00,848
(DOOR OPENING)

336
00:35:00,890 --> 00:35:02,100
(GASPS)

337
00:35:22,829 --> 00:35:24,747
Do not be frightened.

338
00:35:24,831 --> 00:35:26,332
I am not afraid.

339
00:35:27,166 --> 00:35:29,418
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

340
00:35:55,903 --> 00:36:01,617
You know, a couple 
of years ago this would've 
seemed really strange to me.

341
00:36:07,456 --> 00:36:09,917
Lord Imhotep 
will be much pleased.

342
00:36:19,594 --> 00:36:21,220
Where is it?

343
00:36:21,721 --> 00:36:23,931
Where is the bracelet?

344
00:36:24,974 --> 00:36:26,434
I think I know.

345
00:36:27,810 --> 00:36:31,606
At the very top 
of the gold pyramid, 
there was a huge diamond.

346
00:36:31,689 --> 00:36:32,815
Huge? How huge?

347
00:36:32,899 --> 00:36:38,237
It was so big, 
it would reflect the sun 
and wink at distant travelers,

348
00:36:38,279 --> 00:36:40,656
beckoning them 
to their deaths.

349
00:36:42,116 --> 00:36:44,118
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

350
00:37:01,636 --> 00:37:03,930
Get... No! Get off!

351
00:37:07,225 --> 00:37:08,476
Oh, my God.

352
00:37:10,686 --> 00:37:13,522
(SCREAMING)

353
00:37:15,316 --> 00:37:16,525
Rick!

354
00:37:16,817 --> 00:37:18,361
(GUNS FIRING)

355
00:37:27,161 --> 00:37:28,371
Meela!

356
00:38:23,759 --> 00:38:25,344
Go, go, go, go!

357
00:38:40,526 --> 00:38:43,404
Oh, no. 
Not these guys again.

358
00:38:46,198 --> 00:38:48,117
(ALL GROWLING)

359
00:38:55,750 --> 00:38:59,587
Honey, what you doing? 
These guys don't use doors.

360
00:39:02,214 --> 00:39:04,258
Where the hell's Jonathan?

361
00:39:09,847 --> 00:39:11,599
Alex! 
What's the matter 
with my car?

362
00:39:11,682 --> 00:39:14,185
I was forced to find 
an alternative means 
of transportation.

363
00:39:14,226 --> 00:39:16,604
A double-decker bus? 
It was his idea!

364
00:39:16,687 --> 00:39:17,897
Was not! 
Was too!

365
00:39:17,980 --> 00:39:18,981
Just go!

366
00:39:19,065 --> 00:39:20,399
It was too! 
Was not!

367
00:39:20,441 --> 00:39:21,734
Oh, jeez.

368
00:39:35,623 --> 00:39:38,084
No, no! Not my car!

369
00:39:42,505 --> 00:39:45,091
Oh, I hate mummies.

370
00:39:45,174 --> 00:39:48,052
Glad to see me now? 
Just like old times, huh?

371
00:40:07,613 --> 00:40:08,781
Right.

372
00:40:27,800 --> 00:40:29,510
(SNARLING)

373
00:40:45,025 --> 00:40:46,402
(EXCLAIMS)

374
00:40:51,657 --> 00:40:52,908
(SNARLING)

375
00:40:54,535 --> 00:40:55,536
(SCREAMS)

376
00:41:08,883 --> 00:41:10,009
(SNARLING)

377
00:41:15,014 --> 00:41:16,390
(GRUNTING)

378
00:41:25,482 --> 00:41:26,484
(SNARLS)

379
00:41:27,651 --> 00:41:30,863
Turn! Turn! Turn! Turn! Turn!

380
00:41:32,907 --> 00:41:34,325
(YELLING)

381
00:41:41,373 --> 00:41:42,708
(GROWLING)

382
00:41:47,421 --> 00:41:49,798
No! Get out of the way!

383
00:42:10,903 --> 00:42:12,404
(SNARLING)

384
00:42:18,911 --> 00:42:20,454
ALEX: Look out!

385
00:42:26,877 --> 00:42:27,878
(GROWLING)

386
00:42:40,432 --> 00:42:41,767
(GRUNTING)

387
00:42:46,355 --> 00:42:48,941
(GLASS SHATTERING)

388
00:42:48,983 --> 00:42:50,401
Whoa!

389
00:43:23,600 --> 00:43:26,061
Great driving, Uncle Jon. 
Yeah.

390
00:43:33,152 --> 00:43:37,740
You all right? 
This was my first bus ride.

391
00:43:45,122 --> 00:43:46,624
What would I do without you?

392
00:43:46,665 --> 00:43:50,753
Are all librarians 
this much trouble? 
Oh, jeez, get a room.

393
00:44:03,807 --> 00:44:05,643
Let me go! 
Alex!

394
00:44:05,684 --> 00:44:07,436
Silence! 
ALEX: Stop!

395
00:44:07,519 --> 00:44:10,022
Go! 
Stop!

396
00:44:14,360 --> 00:44:16,403
(BELL RINGING)

397
00:44:32,169 --> 00:44:33,504
(GRUNTING)

398
00:44:42,888 --> 00:44:44,223
Alex.

399
00:44:52,106 --> 00:44:54,191
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

400
00:44:57,236 --> 00:44:59,154
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

401
00:45:03,075 --> 00:45:05,035
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

402
00:45:54,626 --> 00:45:57,796
Please, do not fear 
for your son, my friends.

403
00:45:57,880 --> 00:46:01,550
They cannot hurt him, 
for he wears the bracelet 
of Anubis.

404
00:46:01,717 --> 00:46:03,093
Alex is wearing 
the bracelet?

405
00:46:03,135 --> 00:46:06,638
When he put it on, he said 
he saw the pyramids at Giza, 
the temple at Karnak.

406
00:46:06,722 --> 00:46:11,393
And when they reach Karnak, 
the bracelet will show him 
the next step of the journey.

407
00:46:11,477 --> 00:46:12,811
Well, if we don't 
get to Karnak before them,

408
00:46:12,895 --> 00:46:15,564
we won't have any idea 
where to look for him next.

409
00:46:15,647 --> 00:46:19,485
Seems to me like 
we need a magic carpet.

410
00:46:19,818 --> 00:46:21,945
(TRAIN WHISTLE BLOWING)

411
00:46:38,629 --> 00:46:41,215
When Lord Imhotep 
last encountered 
the O'Connells,

412
00:46:41,298 --> 00:46:44,384
they sent his immortal soul 
to the Underworld.

413
00:46:45,010 --> 00:46:48,555
As powerful as he will become, 
he is still vulnerable.

414
00:46:48,639 --> 00:46:52,351
Only with the Army of Anubis 
will he be invincible.

415
00:46:53,519 --> 00:46:55,479
He will need your help.

416
00:46:57,523 --> 00:46:59,191
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

417
00:46:59,233 --> 00:47:01,193
Keep this with you always.

418
00:47:02,361 --> 00:47:03,529
Hey!

419
00:47:03,612 --> 00:47:05,405
<i>The Book of the Dead!</i>

420
00:47:05,489 --> 00:47:07,783
What a bright little child.

421
00:47:09,409 --> 00:47:11,995
Your mother must be 
missing you terribly.

422
00:47:12,037 --> 00:47:14,790
If you wish to see her again, 
you'd better behave.

423
00:47:14,873 --> 00:47:17,292
Lady, I don't behave 
for my parents.

424
00:47:17,376 --> 00:47:19,127
What makes you think 
I'm going to do it for you?

425
00:47:19,211 --> 00:47:20,337
Silence!

426
00:47:20,379 --> 00:47:24,550
Because your parents 
wouldn't slip poisonous snakes 
into your bed

427
00:47:25,050 --> 00:47:27,052
while you were sleeping.

428
00:47:27,761 --> 00:47:30,055
Lord Imhotep 
wishes to meet the boy.

429
00:47:30,931 --> 00:47:33,767
Now we shall see 
how brave you are.

430
00:47:34,768 --> 00:47:37,813
Hey! Watch the suit! Hey!

431
00:47:38,564 --> 00:47:40,107
Me fingers!

432
00:47:41,525 --> 00:47:42,693
Nice.

433
00:47:46,405 --> 00:47:47,948
Very nice.

434
00:47:48,031 --> 00:47:52,244
Did you acquire 
what we asked? 
Oh, we acquired it, all right.

435
00:47:52,536 --> 00:47:53,996
You know what?

436
00:47:54,079 --> 00:47:58,041
We had to kill 
two of those guards at 
the mausoleum to acquire it.

437
00:47:58,083 --> 00:48:00,127
This chest is cursed.

438
00:48:02,212 --> 00:48:08,468
It says there is one, 
the undead, who will kill 
all those who open this chest.

439
00:48:08,552 --> 00:48:10,429
Yes, yes, and the creature 
will suck them dry,

440
00:48:10,470 --> 00:48:12,222
then become whole again.

441
00:48:12,764 --> 00:48:14,141
We've all heard 
this story before.

442
00:48:14,224 --> 00:48:18,145
Yeah, but I heard the yanks 
who found it nine years ago 
all died.

443
00:48:18,228 --> 00:48:20,147
Horrible deaths, they were.

444
00:48:20,606 --> 00:48:23,108
So, with that in mind... 
We want ten.

445
00:48:23,150 --> 00:48:24,234
Quiet!

446
00:48:24,276 --> 00:48:27,237
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

447
00:48:27,904 --> 00:48:29,656
The agreement was for five.

448
00:48:29,740 --> 00:48:32,451
Yeah, well, we want ten, 
or we'll take it elsewhere.

449
00:48:32,534 --> 00:48:35,203
If you... 
Ten will be just fine.

450
00:48:35,287 --> 00:48:36,997
Follow me, gentlemen.

451
00:48:38,957 --> 00:48:40,292
Get in.

452
00:48:46,673 --> 00:48:47,674
(GASPS)

453
00:48:56,141 --> 00:48:58,226
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

454
00:49:02,022 --> 00:49:04,983
It is you 
who are the chosen one,

455
00:49:05,025 --> 00:49:07,903
you who will take me 
to Ahm Shere.

456
00:49:07,986 --> 00:49:12,824
What if I don't? 
What if I get a little... lost?

457
00:49:12,866 --> 00:49:15,118
(LAUGHING)

458
00:49:15,160 --> 00:49:17,788
You have strength, little one.

459
00:49:17,829 --> 00:49:19,998
You are your father's son.

460
00:49:20,082 --> 00:49:22,584
But I know something 
you don't.

461
00:49:22,668 --> 00:49:27,589
This bracelet is a gift 
and a curse.

462
00:49:28,215 --> 00:49:33,720
The sands of time 
have already begun 
to pour against you.

463
00:49:37,516 --> 00:49:39,601
Yeah, yeah. 
I already heard this part.

464
00:49:39,685 --> 00:49:41,228
From the minute 
I put the bracelet on,

465
00:49:41,311 --> 00:49:44,147
seven days do I have before 
the Scorpion King wakes up.

466
00:49:44,189 --> 00:49:46,858
Did you also hear 
that if you do not 
enter the pyramid

467
00:49:46,900 --> 00:49:49,444
before the sun strikes it 
on that very morning

468
00:49:49,528 --> 00:49:52,531
that the bracelet 
will suck the life out of you?

469
00:49:53,490 --> 00:49:55,200
That part I missed.

470
00:49:55,242 --> 00:49:58,245
Hey, wait a minute. 
That means I've only got 
five days left.

471
00:49:58,328 --> 00:50:02,708
Then I believe 
it will be best if we do not 
get lost. Don't you?

472
00:50:02,791 --> 00:50:06,002
My dad 
is going to kick your ass.

473
00:50:11,967 --> 00:50:13,343
(GASPS)

474
00:50:13,635 --> 00:50:15,679
I do not think so.

475
00:50:20,017 --> 00:50:24,104
In here, gentlemen, 
you shall receive 
your just rewards.

476
00:50:24,187 --> 00:50:26,106
No tricks now, woman.

477
00:50:26,481 --> 00:50:28,900
We're not giving up this chest 
till we're satisfied.

478
00:50:28,942 --> 00:50:32,821
Oh, don't worry. 
There is much satisfaction 
to be had.

479
00:50:33,029 --> 00:50:35,073
(WHOOSHING)

480
00:50:41,288 --> 00:50:43,081
What's going on?

481
00:50:47,794 --> 00:50:51,423
This place is cursed.

482
00:50:51,506 --> 00:50:55,260
What is it with you 
and curses? 
He ain't happy 
without a curse.

483
00:50:55,343 --> 00:50:59,514
This is cursed. 
That is cursed. 
Give it a rest, will you!

484
00:50:59,973 --> 00:51:01,892
(ALL SCREAMING)

485
00:51:03,101 --> 00:51:04,394
Christ!

486
00:51:13,153 --> 00:51:16,323
He wants you 
to open the chest! 
Open the chest!

487
00:51:17,032 --> 00:51:18,658
No!

488
00:51:38,053 --> 00:51:40,680
These are the commanders 
of the 12 tribes 
of the Medjai.

489
00:51:42,224 --> 00:51:43,475
Horus!

490
00:51:44,434 --> 00:51:45,894
(CHIRPING)

491
00:51:48,939 --> 00:51:52,359
Pet bird. 
My best 
and most clever friend.

492
00:51:52,776 --> 00:51:55,403
He will let the commanders 
know of our progress 
so that they may follow.

493
00:51:55,403 --> 00:51:57,239
He will let the commanders 
know of our progress 
so that they may follow.

494
00:51:58,573 --> 00:52:00,951
(SPEAKING ARABIC)

495
00:52:04,204 --> 00:52:06,373
(HORSES NEIGHING)

496
00:52:14,005 --> 00:52:16,299
If the Army of Anubis arises,

497
00:52:17,133 --> 00:52:19,761
they will do all they can 
to stop it.

498
00:52:20,095 --> 00:52:24,766
Rick, are you sure 
Izzy's reliable? 
Yeah, yeah, 
he's reliable-ish.

499
00:52:29,688 --> 00:52:32,691
Isn't she beautiful? 
It's a balloon.

500
00:52:32,774 --> 00:52:36,278
Oh! It's a dirigible. 
Where's your airplane?

501
00:52:36,319 --> 00:52:37,737
Airplanes are a thing 
of the past.

502
00:52:38,488 --> 00:52:41,241
Why can't you people 
ever keep your feet 
on the ground?

503
00:53:27,871 --> 00:53:31,791
O'Connell does not want 
to believe, but he flies like 
Horus towards his destiny.

504
00:53:31,875 --> 00:53:35,795
Yes, yes, very interesting. 
Tell me some more 
about this gold pyramid.

505
00:53:35,837 --> 00:53:38,506
Well, it is written 
that since the time 
of the Scorpion King,

506
00:53:38,590 --> 00:53:41,635
no man who has laid eyes 
upon it has ever returned 
to tell the tale.

507
00:53:41,718 --> 00:53:44,471
Where is all 
this stuff written? Hello.

508
00:53:46,431 --> 00:53:47,641
Got it.

509
00:53:48,975 --> 00:53:50,518
(CHIRPING)

510
00:53:53,313 --> 00:53:54,981
Pretty nice, eh?

511
00:53:55,357 --> 00:53:57,400
This is all I have left 
in the world.

512
00:53:57,484 --> 00:53:59,653
The rest of my fortune 
was lost

513
00:53:59,736 --> 00:54:02,322
to some rather 
unscrupulous characters, 
actually.

514
00:54:02,364 --> 00:54:05,784
But if the curator reacted 
to it the way you say, 
it must be very important.

515
00:54:05,825 --> 00:54:08,244
If I were you, 
I would keep it close.

516
00:54:08,328 --> 00:54:11,331
My friend, 
the gods couldn't take this 
away from me.

517
00:54:11,414 --> 00:54:13,959
Hey! That's mine! 
No, it's not!

518
00:54:15,752 --> 00:54:17,837
Keep your hands off of it.

519
00:54:25,679 --> 00:54:26,721
Hey.

520
00:54:27,806 --> 00:54:29,683
I want him back, Rick.

521
00:54:30,600 --> 00:54:33,228
I want him in my arms. 
I know.

522
00:54:36,064 --> 00:54:37,857
We taught him well.

523
00:54:39,067 --> 00:54:40,902
He's smarter than you

524
00:54:42,237 --> 00:54:43,989
and he's tougher than me.

525
00:54:44,072 --> 00:54:48,660
I love him so much. 
I just can't... 
I know. We both do, 
and Alex knows that.

526
00:54:50,578 --> 00:54:53,999
I'll get him back, Evy. 
I promise. 
I know you will.

527
00:55:21,401 --> 00:55:22,736
ALEX: Are we there yet? 
No.

528
00:55:22,819 --> 00:55:24,070
Are we there yet? 
No.

529
00:55:24,112 --> 00:55:25,238
Are we there yet? 
No.

530
00:55:25,280 --> 00:55:26,406
Are we there yet? 
No.

531
00:55:26,448 --> 00:55:27,574
Are we there yet? 
No.

532
00:55:27,615 --> 00:55:28,658
Are we there yet? 
No.

533
00:55:28,742 --> 00:55:29,743
Are we there yet? 
No.

534
00:55:29,826 --> 00:55:30,869
Are we there yet? 
No.

535
00:55:30,910 --> 00:55:32,120
Are we there yet? 
No.

536
00:55:32,203 --> 00:55:33,246
Are we there yet? 
No.

537
00:55:33,288 --> 00:55:34,914
Are we there yet? 
No.

538
00:55:35,915 --> 00:55:37,751
Whoa! That was amazing!

539
00:55:37,834 --> 00:55:40,628
Perfect aim. 
What are you talking about?

540
00:55:42,130 --> 00:55:43,423
I missed.

541
00:55:51,848 --> 00:55:53,516
I have to go to the bathroom.

542
00:56:24,964 --> 00:56:26,508
Make it quick.

543
00:56:33,765 --> 00:56:35,016
Hurry up.

544
00:56:38,561 --> 00:56:41,064
Hey, reading material. 
Now!

545
00:56:45,860 --> 00:56:48,404
I can't go 
when someone's watching.

546
00:56:50,907 --> 00:56:52,492
I don't trust you. 
You'll look.

547
00:56:59,332 --> 00:57:01,543
(GRUNTING)

548
00:57:02,210 --> 00:57:03,420
Damn!

549
00:57:07,590 --> 00:57:11,678
Oh, my God! 
Doesn't anyone around here 
know how to flush a toilet?

550
00:57:30,530 --> 00:57:33,158
(WHEELS SCREECHING)

551
00:57:38,746 --> 00:57:40,540
(MEN CHATTERING)

552
00:57:44,752 --> 00:57:46,379
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

553
00:57:47,046 --> 00:57:48,965
(GUNS FIRING)

554
00:58:12,280 --> 00:58:13,531
Karnak.

555
00:58:26,085 --> 00:58:27,128
Huh?

556
00:58:48,524 --> 00:58:50,693
(CHIRPING)

557
00:58:54,447 --> 00:58:57,492
If a man does not 
embrace his past, 
he has no future.

558
00:58:57,575 --> 00:59:01,329
Look, even if

559
00:59:01,871 --> 00:59:05,583
I was some sort of 
sacred Medjai, what good 
does that do me now?

560
00:59:05,667 --> 00:59:07,794
It is the missing piece 
of your heart.

561
00:59:08,002 --> 00:59:11,589
If you embrace it, 
if you accept it, 
you can do anything.

562
00:59:12,006 --> 00:59:13,841
Sounds great. Listen.

563
00:59:14,300 --> 00:59:17,303
What can we expect 
from our old friend Imhotep?

564
00:59:17,345 --> 00:59:19,389
His powers are returning.

565
00:59:19,472 --> 00:59:20,598
By the time 
he reaches Ahm Shere,

566
00:59:20,640 --> 00:59:22,684
even the Scorpion King 
won't be able to stop him.

567
00:59:37,156 --> 00:59:41,119
<i>(IMHOTEP SPEAKING 
ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)</i>

568
01:00:11,733 --> 01:00:13,651
(MAN SPEAKING 
ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

569
01:00:45,516 --> 01:00:49,228
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

570
01:01:54,210 --> 01:01:56,295
(ALL CLAPPING)

571
01:02:11,144 --> 01:02:14,897
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

572
01:03:40,566 --> 01:03:42,485
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

573
01:03:43,903 --> 01:03:45,655
PHARAOH: Anck-su-namun!

574
01:03:58,417 --> 01:03:59,669
Imhotep!

575
01:04:00,836 --> 01:04:03,089
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

576
01:04:11,639 --> 01:04:13,474
(SCREAMING)

577
01:04:13,766 --> 01:04:14,892
Evy!

578
01:04:17,186 --> 01:04:18,187
(BOTH GRUNTING)

579
01:04:39,792 --> 01:04:41,043
Imhotep!

580
01:05:12,992 --> 01:05:15,494
Imhotep. 
Anck-su-namun.

581
01:05:23,294 --> 01:05:25,504
Evy, I know 
you haven't exactly 
been yourself lately

582
01:05:25,546 --> 01:05:27,173
with all these dreams 
and visions...

583
01:05:27,214 --> 01:05:29,759
No, no, 
they're memories 
from my previous life.

584
01:05:29,842 --> 01:05:32,720
Honestly, I'm not 
losing my mind. It all 
makes perfect sense now.

585
01:05:32,845 --> 01:05:34,680
And that's the reason 
why we found the bracelet?

586
01:05:34,764 --> 01:05:36,724
Exactly. I was its protector.

587
01:05:36,807 --> 01:05:38,351
Now do you believe, 
my friend?

588
01:05:38,392 --> 01:05:40,645
Clearly, you were destined 
to protect this woman.

589
01:05:40,686 --> 01:05:44,148
Right. 
She's a reincarnated princess, 
and I'm a warrior for God.

590
01:05:44,190 --> 01:05:48,402
And your son leads the way 
to Ahm Shere. 
Three sides of the pyramid.

591
01:05:48,527 --> 01:05:51,197
This was all preordained 
thousands of years ago.

592
01:05:51,280 --> 01:05:52,907
And how does the story end?

593
01:05:52,990 --> 01:05:56,077
Only the journey's written, 
not the destination.

594
01:05:56,160 --> 01:05:59,163
Convenient. 
How else do you explain 
Evy's visions?

595
01:05:59,205 --> 01:06:01,832
That it is your son 
who wears the bracelet?

596
01:06:01,874 --> 01:06:04,502
How do you explain your mark? 
Coincidence.

597
01:06:04,669 --> 01:06:09,090
My friend, 
there is a fine line between 
coincidence and fate.

598
01:06:29,318 --> 01:06:31,404
Don't even think about it!

599
01:06:35,157 --> 01:06:37,076
Hold on there, partner.

600
01:06:40,454 --> 01:06:42,248
When the time comes,

601
01:06:43,249 --> 01:06:45,626
I shall truly 
enjoy killing you.

602
01:06:47,586 --> 01:06:49,380
But until that time,

603
01:06:50,339 --> 01:06:52,883
you better be 
a little nicer to me.

604
01:06:53,217 --> 01:06:55,094
Now, where's my water?

605
01:06:59,098 --> 01:07:00,307
No ice?

606
01:07:03,019 --> 01:07:04,770
(SPEAKING 
ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

607
01:07:05,730 --> 01:07:07,773
Make sure he doesn't move!

608
01:07:38,053 --> 01:07:40,306
They've gone. We've lost them.

609
01:07:56,614 --> 01:07:57,698
Rick!

610
01:08:06,916 --> 01:08:08,709
Alex left us his tie,

611
01:08:09,335 --> 01:08:12,713
and he made us 
a little sand castle.

612
01:08:13,589 --> 01:08:15,674
It's the Temple Island 
of Philae.

613
01:08:15,716 --> 01:08:17,635
They've gone to Philae. 
That-a-boy, Alex.

614
01:08:17,676 --> 01:08:18,969
Come on!

615
01:08:30,689 --> 01:08:33,025
The great temple 
of Abu Simbel.

616
01:08:33,359 --> 01:08:35,027
(CHIRPING)

617
01:09:35,963 --> 01:09:38,883
(SPEAKING ARABIC)

618
01:10:00,446 --> 01:10:02,781
That's the Blue Nile 
down there.

619
01:10:02,907 --> 01:10:04,408
We must be 
out of Egypt by now.

620
01:10:04,450 --> 01:10:07,912
In ancient times, 
all this still belonged 
to the upper kingdom.

621
01:10:08,329 --> 01:10:10,539
The oasis must be 
around here somewhere.

622
01:10:10,623 --> 01:10:13,542
RICK: Don't worry, Evy, 
we'll find him. 
He's a smart kid.

623
01:10:13,626 --> 01:10:15,502
He'll leave us a sign.

624
01:10:20,716 --> 01:10:22,509
Surprised to see me?

625
01:10:23,177 --> 01:10:25,804
Leaving bread crumbs, 
huh? Huh?

626
01:10:26,138 --> 01:10:30,726
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

627
01:11:12,518 --> 01:11:13,519
(GASPS)

628
01:11:19,650 --> 01:11:22,111
We're in trouble!

629
01:11:23,112 --> 01:11:24,238
Whoa!

630
01:11:27,449 --> 01:11:28,784
(GROWLING)

631
01:11:34,415 --> 01:11:35,833
Horus, fly!

632
01:11:38,627 --> 01:11:42,715
Izzy, come hard right! 
Starboard! Starboard!

633
01:11:42,798 --> 01:11:44,425
(GRUNTING)

634
01:12:17,291 --> 01:12:20,044
(ALL PANTING)

635
01:12:25,883 --> 01:12:28,635
Was there a little something 
you forgot to mention?

636
01:12:33,390 --> 01:12:34,600
People?

637
01:12:42,524 --> 01:12:44,401
(BIRDS TWITTERING)

638
01:12:46,695 --> 01:12:49,031
(MONKEYS CHATTERING)

639
01:12:53,786 --> 01:12:55,120
Ahm Shere.

640
01:13:06,131 --> 01:13:07,341
Right.

641
01:13:07,424 --> 01:13:09,510
(RUMBLING)

642
01:13:14,306 --> 01:13:15,391
He's back!

643
01:13:15,516 --> 01:13:17,142
(GROWLING)

644
01:13:19,144 --> 01:13:20,437
Hang on!

645
01:13:34,243 --> 01:13:36,120
Well, that's not good.

646
01:13:37,663 --> 01:13:38,914
RICK: Hang on!

647
01:13:46,505 --> 01:13:47,589
Mom?

648
01:13:48,674 --> 01:13:49,758
Dad?

649
01:13:59,685 --> 01:14:01,186
RICK: 
We're gonna go get my son.

650
01:14:01,270 --> 01:14:02,896
Then we're gonna wanna 
get out of here fast,

651
01:14:02,980 --> 01:14:04,106
so make this work, Izzy. 
No, no, you don't understand, 
goddamn it.

652
01:14:08,694 --> 01:14:10,237
Come to Daddy.

653
01:14:12,197 --> 01:14:13,490
(WHISTLING)

654
01:14:13,574 --> 01:14:14,741
Horus!

655
01:14:14,825 --> 01:14:17,536
(CHIRPING)

656
01:14:23,542 --> 01:14:27,254
JONATHAN: So, Rick, 
what's the plan? 
RICK: Let's find 
some higher ground.

657
01:14:32,217 --> 01:14:35,095
(HORUS CHIRPING)

658
01:14:44,354 --> 01:14:45,814
(GUN FIRES)

659
01:14:46,565 --> 01:14:47,774
Horus!

660
01:14:54,364 --> 01:14:55,991
I must go. 
Where?

661
01:14:56,074 --> 01:14:57,618
I must let the commanders 
know where we are.

662
01:14:57,659 --> 01:14:59,536
You can't go. 
If the Army 
of Anubis arises...

663
01:14:59,620 --> 01:15:02,080
I need you 
to help me find my son.

664
01:15:07,461 --> 01:15:10,005
Then first, I shall help you. 
Thank you.

665
01:15:20,974 --> 01:15:22,935
(CRICKETS CHIRPING)

666
01:15:49,002 --> 01:15:51,338
Look. Roman legionnaires.

667
01:15:53,882 --> 01:15:57,678
And here. 
Turn-of-the-century French. 
Napoleon's troops.

668
01:15:57,761 --> 01:16:00,347
What in the name 
of Anubis did this?

669
01:16:08,355 --> 01:16:10,566
(GROWLING)

670
01:16:21,368 --> 01:16:23,203
You hear that? 
What?

671
01:16:24,580 --> 01:16:25,872
Nothing.

672
01:16:26,832 --> 01:16:28,583
Absolutely nothing.

673
01:16:33,046 --> 01:16:34,548
You any good with that?

674
01:16:34,798 --> 01:16:37,801
Three times Fox and Hound's 
grand champion, 
I'll have you know.

675
01:16:37,884 --> 01:16:41,346
You any good with that? 
You'll know soon enough.

676
01:16:45,892 --> 01:16:48,312
Evy, try to remember to...

677
01:16:49,980 --> 01:16:52,733
Just keep it tight 
in the shoulder and

678
01:16:54,651 --> 01:16:57,446
lead the target a little bit, 
and then...

679
01:16:58,614 --> 01:17:01,116
And squeeze the trigger. 
Don't pull it.

680
01:17:02,951 --> 01:17:04,453
I won't miss.

681
01:17:29,436 --> 01:17:31,563
(SNARLING)

682
01:17:44,201 --> 01:17:46,328
Pyramid. 
The pyramid.

683
01:17:47,037 --> 01:17:49,164
Cripes, I'm in trouble now.

684
01:17:49,539 --> 01:17:51,333
Now may I kill him?

685
01:17:51,958 --> 01:17:54,169
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

686
01:18:04,179 --> 01:18:06,640
Retrieve that bracelet. 
With pleasure.

687
01:18:20,070 --> 01:18:22,030
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

688
01:18:24,700 --> 01:18:26,743
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

689
01:18:32,958 --> 01:18:35,669
Something is coming.

690
01:18:49,224 --> 01:18:51,101
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

691
01:18:56,606 --> 01:18:58,191
Jonathan? 
Yes?

692
01:18:58,817 --> 01:19:01,570
That's my husband 
and my son down there.

693
01:19:01,903 --> 01:19:03,447
Make me proud.

694
01:19:04,448 --> 01:19:06,366
Today's that day, Evy.

695
01:19:06,741 --> 01:19:07,909
(GUN COCKING)

696
01:19:12,998 --> 01:19:14,416
(MAN SHOUTING IN ARABIC)

697
01:19:14,499 --> 01:19:16,084
Where's the boy?

698
01:20:20,732 --> 01:20:22,317
The black book!

699
01:20:27,322 --> 01:20:28,657
Let's go!

700
01:20:29,699 --> 01:20:32,160
(PEOPLE YELLING)

701
01:20:34,955 --> 01:20:36,623
(MEN SHOUTING)

702
01:20:58,270 --> 01:20:59,813
There you are!

703
01:20:59,855 --> 01:21:01,856
(GUNS FIRING)

704
01:21:02,399 --> 01:21:05,944
The time has come, 
my little friend. 
Let go!

705
01:21:19,457 --> 01:21:22,002
Dad! 
Alex!

706
01:21:23,461 --> 01:21:24,671
Alex...

707
01:21:32,095 --> 01:21:33,138
Dad!

708
01:21:42,647 --> 01:21:45,483
Time to remove that bracelet, 
my good son.

709
01:21:45,650 --> 01:21:46,735
Dad!

710
01:21:56,036 --> 01:21:58,580
Dad, behind you! 
Whoa!

711
01:22:04,377 --> 01:22:05,962
(YELLING)

712
01:22:14,763 --> 01:22:16,222
(MEN GRUNTING)

713
01:22:21,186 --> 01:22:22,854
(MEN EXCLAIMING)

714
01:22:28,568 --> 01:22:30,028
(SNARLING)

715
01:23:08,316 --> 01:23:09,859
(GUN FIRES)

716
01:23:21,788 --> 01:23:24,124
Let's go. 
Thank God for that.

717
01:23:31,297 --> 01:23:35,260
The two of you must 
sacrifice yourselves for me.

718
01:23:36,261 --> 01:23:38,638
You shall be rewarded 
in heaven!

719
01:23:44,769 --> 01:23:46,229
(SNARLING)

720
01:23:53,820 --> 01:23:55,238
Mom! 
Alex!

721
01:23:56,531 --> 01:23:57,615
Hey, nice shootin', Tex.

722
01:23:57,699 --> 01:23:59,826
What were those creepy 
little pygmy things?

723
01:23:59,909 --> 01:24:02,120
Just the local natives. 
Are you sure?

724
01:24:02,203 --> 01:24:03,455
I'm sure. It was nothin'.

725
01:24:03,538 --> 01:24:05,540
Come on, Mom! 
Come on! Come on, Dad!

726
01:24:05,623 --> 01:24:08,960
We have to get to the pyramid. 
I have to get the bracelet 
off now!

727
01:24:09,002 --> 01:24:11,046
Oh, leave it on, Alex. 
Looks good on you.

728
01:24:11,129 --> 01:24:13,131
No, you guys! 
You don't understand!

729
01:24:13,173 --> 01:24:14,883
He told me the bracelet 
will kill me

730
01:24:14,966 --> 01:24:17,802
if I don't get inside 
the pyramid 
before the sun hits it!

731
01:24:17,886 --> 01:24:20,430
Today! 
Oh, my God.

732
01:24:20,555 --> 01:24:22,724
(CREATURES SCREECHING)

733
01:24:24,142 --> 01:24:25,560
Time to go!

734
01:24:31,524 --> 01:24:33,151
(SCREECHING)

735
01:24:42,452 --> 01:24:45,413
JONATHAN: Wait for me! 
EVELYN: Hurry up, Jonathan!

736
01:24:46,664 --> 01:24:49,209
Wait for me! What's that for?

737
01:24:49,375 --> 01:24:51,878
Ah, nothin'. 
Just a little something 
in case of an emergency.

738
01:24:52,962 --> 01:24:54,380
(SCREECHING)

739
01:25:09,979 --> 01:25:11,106
Rick.

740
01:25:14,901 --> 01:25:16,486
Let's go, Alex!

741
01:25:25,620 --> 01:25:29,082
Run! Come on, Alex, 
faster! Come on!

742
01:25:29,457 --> 01:25:32,710
Come on! 
Dad! The bracelet!

743
01:25:32,877 --> 01:25:34,838
Run! Come on!

744
01:25:53,189 --> 01:25:54,732
(BOTH PANTING)

745
01:25:57,861 --> 01:26:00,363
You know, it's not

746
01:26:00,864 --> 01:26:02,866
easy being a dad.

747
01:26:04,284 --> 01:26:06,953
Yeah, 
but you do it really good.

748
01:26:08,288 --> 01:26:09,539
Thanks.

749
01:26:28,641 --> 01:26:31,144
They made it. Thank God.

750
01:26:32,228 --> 01:26:34,105
Oh, yes. Great.

751
01:26:34,814 --> 01:26:36,107
Fabulous.

752
01:26:37,150 --> 01:26:38,318
(GROANS)

753
01:26:39,694 --> 01:26:40,778
No!

754
01:26:53,625 --> 01:26:54,709
Evy!

755
01:26:55,168 --> 01:26:56,252
Evy!

756
01:27:01,674 --> 01:27:03,718
Jonathan! Jonathan! 
Mom!

757
01:27:05,011 --> 01:27:07,972
You're going to be all right. 
Isn't she, Dad? 
She'll be fine.

758
01:27:08,014 --> 01:27:10,725
She's going to be all right. 
Just get him... 
Take him. Take...

759
01:27:10,808 --> 01:27:12,769
Mommy's fine. It's okay.

760
01:27:14,020 --> 01:27:16,022
Where... Evy... 
Your mother's 
gonna be fine, okay?

761
01:27:16,064 --> 01:27:17,690
Oh, my God!

762
01:27:18,483 --> 01:27:21,194
You're real strong. 
You're gonna make it. 
You're gonna make it.

763
01:27:21,277 --> 01:27:22,695
RICK: You're fine.

764
01:27:23,237 --> 01:27:26,699
What do I do? 
What do I do, Evy?

765
01:27:27,367 --> 01:27:30,328
What do I do? 
Take care of Alex.

766
01:27:32,538 --> 01:27:35,875
No. Sweetheart, no.

767
01:27:38,211 --> 01:27:39,587
I love you.

768
01:27:41,172 --> 01:27:44,425
No, don't... No. No!

769
01:27:45,718 --> 01:27:47,303
Evy? Evy?

770
01:27:48,596 --> 01:27:52,642
RICK: No. No. Evy!

771
01:27:57,105 --> 01:27:58,898
Come back, Evy.

772
01:28:00,984 --> 01:28:02,902
Evy, come back.

773
01:28:04,070 --> 01:28:05,405
Come back.

774
01:28:53,619 --> 01:28:55,788
(BOTH SCREAMING)

775
01:29:16,434 --> 01:29:18,436
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

776
01:29:30,823 --> 01:29:32,200
Stay here.

777
01:29:43,544 --> 01:29:44,754
(GASPS)

778
01:29:46,005 --> 01:29:48,383
(SKITTERING)

779
01:30:24,293 --> 01:30:25,420
Whoa!

780
01:31:00,371 --> 01:31:02,415
(SPEAKING ARABIC)

781
01:31:07,086 --> 01:31:09,589
Try to think of it like this, 
Alex.

782
01:31:09,922 --> 01:31:12,175
She's gone to a better place.

783
01:31:12,341 --> 01:31:14,260
You know, 
like it says in the good book.

784
01:31:14,302 --> 01:31:15,928
The book. 
What?

785
01:31:16,012 --> 01:31:17,180
That's it.

786
01:31:17,263 --> 01:31:19,974
That's it. Come on, 
Uncle Jon! 
That's what?

787
01:31:20,057 --> 01:31:21,893
Come on! Come on! 
That's it! The book! 
What?

788
01:31:21,934 --> 01:31:23,686
(GRUNTING)

789
01:31:31,319 --> 01:31:35,281
You're too late, O'Connell. 
I have released 
the Army of Anubis.

790
01:31:36,032 --> 01:31:40,244
Lord Imhotep shall soon kill 
the Scorpion King 
and take command.

791
01:31:41,329 --> 01:31:42,830
Not after 
I get through with him.

792
01:31:49,504 --> 01:31:51,964
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

793
01:31:59,013 --> 01:32:00,097
<i>Niy!</i>

794
01:32:08,522 --> 01:32:11,108
<i>Niy! Niy!</i>

795
01:32:11,859 --> 01:32:13,277
You realize, of course,

796
01:32:13,361 --> 01:32:17,073
that this can only be done 
by someone who can actually 
read ancient Egyptian.

797
01:32:17,156 --> 01:32:20,117
I don't know about you, 
but I'm a tad rusty.

798
01:32:21,202 --> 01:32:22,578
Now where?

799
01:32:22,703 --> 01:32:25,039
We go right. 
How do you know?

800
01:32:26,040 --> 01:32:28,000
<i>"Kasheesh Osirian Nye."</i>

801
01:32:28,543 --> 01:32:31,587
Basically, "This way 
to the Scorpion King."

802
01:32:33,130 --> 01:32:34,674
Mum taught me.

803
01:32:37,969 --> 01:32:39,804
This just might work.

804
01:33:04,620 --> 01:33:06,247
(GROWLING)

805
01:33:08,791 --> 01:33:10,835
(JONATHAN CLEARING THROAT)

806
01:33:10,918 --> 01:33:13,212
It's time someone 
taught you a lesson, 
wench. Come on.

807
01:33:22,179 --> 01:33:24,098
This is for my sister.

808
01:33:26,976 --> 01:33:28,436
(GONG RINGING)

809
01:33:50,082 --> 01:33:51,500
(GRUNTING)

810
01:34:02,136 --> 01:34:03,512
(GRUNTING)

811
01:34:15,483 --> 01:34:17,318
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

812
01:34:49,183 --> 01:34:50,601
(GROWLING)

813
01:34:56,565 --> 01:34:59,068
(YELLING)

814
01:35:13,499 --> 01:35:15,418
Is that all you've got?

815
01:35:22,675 --> 01:35:25,052
(SHOUTING)

816
01:35:25,094 --> 01:35:27,012
(ALL YELLING)

817
01:36:07,344 --> 01:36:08,888
Hurry up, Alex!

818
01:36:09,138 --> 01:36:13,642
<i>"Hootash naraba oos Veesloo.</i>

819
01:36:14,143 --> 01:36:17,188
<i>"Ahm kum Ra. Ahm kum Dei."</i>

820
01:37:00,147 --> 01:37:03,400
<i>"Efday Shokran... 
Efday Shokran..."</i>

821
01:37:03,484 --> 01:37:06,278
Uncle Jon, I don't know 
what this last symbol is!

822
01:37:06,487 --> 01:37:09,865
What's it look like? 
It's a bird! A stork!

823
01:37:12,535 --> 01:37:14,995
I know that one! 
I know that one!

824
01:37:15,579 --> 01:37:17,206
Then what is it?

825
01:37:19,500 --> 01:37:20,918
<i>Ahmenophus!</i>

826
01:37:22,002 --> 01:37:25,256
That's it! 
<i>"Efday Shokran Ahmenophus!"</i>

827
01:38:06,380 --> 01:38:09,341
Why don't you pick on 
somebody your own size?

828
01:38:09,675 --> 01:38:12,469
Oh, my God. Evy! 
Take Alex.

829
01:38:12,553 --> 01:38:14,388
Go and help Rick. 
But Mom...

830
01:38:14,430 --> 01:38:15,598
No "buts," Alex.

831
01:38:15,681 --> 01:38:17,891
Come on, Alex. 
But... But...

832
01:38:19,727 --> 01:38:21,437
I'll be just fine.

833
01:38:21,729 --> 01:38:23,647
We did it, Uncle Jon! 
We did it!

834
01:38:23,731 --> 01:38:25,733
Right, partner. 
Now, let's go help your dad.

835
01:39:20,496 --> 01:39:22,247
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

836
01:39:34,301 --> 01:39:35,719
(GROWLING)

837
01:40:02,287 --> 01:40:03,664
Nefertiri.

838
01:40:05,165 --> 01:40:06,667
Anck-su-namun.

839
01:40:07,334 --> 01:40:09,003
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

840
01:40:28,188 --> 01:40:30,232
That's a little 
something new!

841
01:40:55,466 --> 01:40:57,551
(ALL CHEERING)

842
01:41:17,780 --> 01:41:19,239
(ALL SHOUTING)

843
01:41:33,462 --> 01:41:35,172
(SPEAKING ARABIC)

844
01:42:02,658 --> 01:42:04,660
Okay, now I'm a believer.

845
01:42:05,661 --> 01:42:06,787
Rick!

846
01:42:08,831 --> 01:42:10,457
Jonathan! 
Dad!

847
01:42:10,958 --> 01:42:12,125
It's a spear!

848
01:42:12,167 --> 01:42:14,837
The gold stick thing... 
It's a... It's a spear!

849
01:42:14,920 --> 01:42:17,798
Really? 
Doesn't look like a spear!

850
01:42:17,881 --> 01:42:21,009
No! That's because 
it opens up into one!

851
01:42:21,093 --> 01:42:23,137
Yes? And? 
Jonathan!

852
01:42:23,178 --> 01:42:26,348
It opens up into a spear!

853
01:42:26,431 --> 01:42:28,433
(ROARING)

854
01:42:31,812 --> 01:42:33,522
(BOTH SCREAMING)

855
01:42:55,544 --> 01:42:57,504
(SPEAKING ARABIC)

856
01:42:57,546 --> 01:42:59,840
(ALL SHOUTING)

857
01:43:12,769 --> 01:43:15,689
Rick! 
Evy?

858
01:43:22,237 --> 01:43:24,698
Twist it! 
Pull! I tried it! Push!

859
01:43:27,200 --> 01:43:28,577
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

860
01:43:28,660 --> 01:43:30,287
Jonathan, quick!

861
01:43:44,259 --> 01:43:47,387
Jonathan, throw it! 
Kill the Scorpion King!

862
01:43:47,471 --> 01:43:49,556
Send his army back 
to the Underworld!

863
01:43:50,223 --> 01:43:52,517
Step aside, Alex. 
I'm a professional.

864
01:44:03,236 --> 01:44:04,905
(SNARLING)

865
01:44:07,574 --> 01:44:10,077
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

866
01:44:12,412 --> 01:44:13,538
Rick!

867
01:44:21,463 --> 01:44:23,257
No!

868
01:44:42,734 --> 01:44:43,777
No!

869
01:44:45,112 --> 01:44:46,530
(GROWLING)

870
01:44:49,032 --> 01:44:50,534
<i>Niy!</i>

871
01:44:56,498 --> 01:44:59,918
Go to hell, and take 
your friends with you!

872
01:45:01,795 --> 01:45:03,297
(GROWLING)

873
01:45:22,816 --> 01:45:24,985
(ALL CHEERING)

874
01:45:56,016 --> 01:45:57,351
(GRUNTS)

875
01:46:04,566 --> 01:46:05,942
(GRUNTS)

876
01:46:14,034 --> 01:46:15,243
(GRUNTS)

877
01:46:16,453 --> 01:46:17,537
Dad!

878
01:46:35,514 --> 01:46:38,725
Evy, no! Get out of here!

879
01:46:39,017 --> 01:46:40,852
Just get out of here!

880
01:46:41,645 --> 01:46:42,729
No!

881
01:46:47,234 --> 01:46:48,318
Mom!

882
01:47:01,748 --> 01:47:02,833
Hang on, Rick!

883
01:47:06,753 --> 01:47:08,213
(SCREAMS)

884
01:47:13,301 --> 01:47:14,845
Anck-su-namun!

885
01:47:19,516 --> 01:47:22,602
No! 
Anck-su-namun!

886
01:47:27,023 --> 01:47:28,567
Anck-su-namun.

887
01:47:45,041 --> 01:47:46,626
(GROWLING)

888
01:47:50,547 --> 01:47:51,464
(RUMBLING)

889
01:47:53,967 --> 01:47:55,093
Whoa!

890
01:47:59,973 --> 01:48:01,433
Let's go up!

891
01:48:20,994 --> 01:48:23,246
This whole damn place 
is gonna get sucked up!

892
01:48:23,330 --> 01:48:24,998
Let's move up! Go!

893
01:48:38,345 --> 01:48:40,472
JONATHAN: Go, Alex! 
Come on! Come on!

894
01:48:51,024 --> 01:48:52,859
Rick, we're trapped!

895
01:49:00,367 --> 01:49:01,451
IZZY: Hey!

896
01:49:04,704 --> 01:49:07,582
Izzy! 
Come on! 
Get your butts moving!

897
01:49:07,666 --> 01:49:09,876
Hurry up! Hurry up! 
I haven't got all day!

898
01:49:14,297 --> 01:49:15,924
RICK: Go! You're next!

899
01:49:21,263 --> 01:49:22,889
Right.

900
01:49:39,739 --> 01:49:41,366
Izzy! Thank you!

901
01:49:42,867 --> 01:49:45,453
O'Connell, who the hell 
you been messin' with 
this time?

902
01:49:45,495 --> 01:49:47,289
Huh? 
Oh, you know, the usual.

903
01:49:47,330 --> 01:49:49,541
Mummies, pygmies,

904
01:49:50,292 --> 01:49:51,585
big bugs.

905
01:50:01,636 --> 01:50:03,513
(SPEAKING ARABIC)

906
01:50:12,105 --> 01:50:13,815
(HORSE NEIGHING)

907
01:50:20,822 --> 01:50:23,283
I thought 
I almost lost you there.

908
01:50:23,825 --> 01:50:25,744
For a moment there, you did.

909
01:50:27,037 --> 01:50:29,456
Would you like to know 
what heaven looks like?

910
01:50:30,915 --> 01:50:32,083
Later.

911
01:50:36,087 --> 01:50:37,881
BOTH: Oh, please!

912
01:50:38,214 --> 01:50:40,675
That's half mine, 
you know. 
What?

913
01:50:40,759 --> 01:50:43,178
That's half mine. 
I have no idea 
what you're talking about.

914
01:50:43,219 --> 01:50:46,348
What? You took my gold stick! 
I know you took my gold stick!

915
01:50:46,389 --> 01:50:50,602
I swear on the head 
of my wife, I have no idea 
what you're talking about.

916
01:50:50,685 --> 01:50:52,687
IZZY: You haven't... 
You ain't got a wife!

917
01:50:52,729 --> 01:50:55,273
JONATHAN: I don't have 
your gold stick either!
